                <pb facs="0246" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1217: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-19T13:00:00+08:00">July 19, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 19—12:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>593. Legation’s 561, July 10, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m. Following
                    from American Consul General at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“On July 16 American missionaries again evacuated Yochow and are on board
                            gunboat and Socony’s <hi rendition="#italic">Mei Ping</hi> at
                            Chenglingki.</p>
                        <p>Hankow situation quiet.</p>
                        <p>Hunan is now entirely under Ho Chien who commands four divisions of
                            reduced strength.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
